 "notes": "FOSILLY #56, boss card: no exit; win by entering the skull Lair (front centre) in the sword sequence. Vine paths cross over each other; crossings treated as bridges (no connection) unless the cream areas merge. Doubts: front start strip assumed to reach only door (0.53,0.20); unsure whether the long vine below it (y~0.27, left room to right room) also touches the door's bottom. Skull tentacles at (0.33,0.65), (0.52,0.70) and (0.65,0.70) assumed to join the Lair. Front door (0.78,0.75) modelled as linking the lower-right vine junction with the right strip. Back: central hub (top stem + both upper vines) assumed separate from the vine at y~0.43 below the drips. Plausible route only works if a top/bottom flip turns the card 180 deg on screen (all spins sit behind non-up doors when upright): start, door up, top flip, back hub, door (down) to spinNW...",
